{"results":[{"url":"https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000006597776/trump-speech-airports.html","final_url":"https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000006597776/trump-speech-airports.html","title":"Video: Trump Says Revolutionary War-Era Army ‘Took Over the Airports’","description":"The president’s anachronism came during his Fourth of July speech, as he bounced from describing the Revolutionary War to the War of 1812.","language":"en","text":"new video loaded: Trump Says Revolutionary War-Era Army ‘Took Over the Airports’\n\ntranscript\n\n## Trump Says Revolutionary War-Era Army ‘Took Over the Airports’\n\n#### The president’s anachronism came during his Fourth of July speech, as he bounced from describing the Revolutionary War to the War of 1812.\n\n* In June of 1775, the Continental Congress created a unified Army out of the revolutionary forces encamped around Boston and New York — and named after the great George Washington, commander in chief. Our Army manned the air, it rammed the ramparts, it took over the airports. It did everything it had to do. And at Fort McHenry, under the rockets’ red glare, it had nothing but victory. And when dawn came, their star-spangled banner waved defiant.\n\n# Trump Says Revolutionary War-Era Army ‘Took Over the Airports’\n\nThe president’s anachronism came during his Fourth of July speech, as he bounced from describing the Revolutionary War to the War of 1812.\n\nBy C-Span/associated Press\n\nJuly 5, 2019","author":null,"published_date":"2019-07-05T18:47:01.000Z","latency_ms":8994.324372994015,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}